      "content": "That thought of giving up because the fight feels unfair is a very heavy and understandable feeling when exhaustion becomes the only truth you know. Please know that feeling like your story has ended doesn't mean it has actually ended, and that \"logical\" decision to stop is often a symptom of the illness protecting you rather than a plan for your future. You are not responsible for saving everyone around you, and your worth is not tied to your energy levels or your ability to perform. If the urge to stop feels too strong to bare alone, reaching out to a crisis line is an act of bravery, not surrender.",
